  "id": "COMPOUND:14884 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Borapetoside D is implicated in the pathway leading to CX-1 through multiple intermediate targets, all of which are found in hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that Borapetoside D directly targets hepatocytes, which in turn are targets of various compounds, including (4S,5S)-5-[(1R,2R)-2-Hydroxy-2-Methyl-5-Oxocyclopent-3-En-1-Yl]-3-Methylidene-4-(3-Oxobutyl)Oxolan-2-One and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These intermediates are all capable of targeting CX-1, indicating a potential chain of interactions where Borapetoside D influences the biological process through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Borapetoside D may modulate cellular activity, ultimately affecting CX-1. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Borapetoside D and CX-1 through a series of molecular targets in hepatocytes, emphasizing the role of these intermediates in the overall biological response.",
